From 10b8c130afe0b33b6db336b676766fed46f0eb87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: STX Hardening <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:43:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Production hardening: provisioning, checkout, payment
 proofs, compose

- Rewrite ProvisionPaidServerJob: queue-only, unique per order, row-locked claim,
  Pelican node/allocation selection, no invented nodes, no direct-DB server fallback,
  no hardcoded DB root password, idempotent via server external_id
- Approve/Retry now queue the job; approval is atomic (HostingOrder::approveAndQueueProvisioning)
- Checkout: validation, active payment method, region allow-list, session regeneration,
  no raw exception messages, no email enumeration, open-order cap
- Payment proofs: extension from real MIME, duplicate-slip detection, safe download headers,
  block proofs on completed/cancelled orders, fix viewPaymentProof permission check
- Rate limits on checkout, proof upload, contact, status/KB APIs
- Contact form actually sends mail instead of faking a ticket
- Add hosting:expire-orders (hourly) to expire unpaid orders
- docker-compose: remove missing status-page build, require secrets, drop source bind mounts,
  healthchecks, remove invalid MariaDB flag; add .env.example
- README: remove nonexistent default credentials, add production checklist
- Remove dead duplicate command and unsafe scripts/test_provision.php
