From: STX Hardening <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:44:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Status page and invoice: rebuild and fix misleading data

- /api/status/ping is now read-only; it used to run every monitor probe on each public request
- Status timeline no longer invents 'operational' history for windows with no checks
- Seeded monitor names no longer claim 'High-Availability' / 'Distributed' infrastructure
- Status page rebuilt: real uptime/latency/history, range links instead of JS buttons,
  filter, and a working auto-refresh (the old script only logged to the console)
- Invoice: number was derived from the current year so it changed every January; now uses the
  order number. Rebuilt as a self-contained printable document with setup fee, discount and
  paid/awaiting/cancelled status from real order data
